{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772650840,"nonce":"x7fTbuYvptWF//wgH+bA/Pryjho=","title":"auth-request.sh: misleading Mandible unreachable when API returns error status","message":"When the POST to /api/auth/request returns a non-2xx response, curl -sf exits non-zero and the script falls into the \"Mandible unreachable\" fallback path — even though Mandible is running fine. The actual API error is silently swallowed.\n\nFix: capture curl response and HTTP status separately (use -w '%{http_code}' without -f), print the API error body on failure, only fall back to terminal pane on connection-level failure (exit code 7/28).\n\nMigrated from dotfiles issue e5a2aec.","files":null}]}